\li1 
\v 18 \zwd Caleb son of \zwd Hezron|id="Q4177234" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q16938772" t="2"\zwd* had children by \zwd his wife Azubah|id="Q139582293" t="2"\zwd* and by \zwd Jerioth|\zwd*. These were the sons of \zwd Azubah|id="Q139582293" t="2"\zwd*: \zwd Jesher|\zwd*, \zwd Shobab|\zwd*, and \zwd Ardon|id="Q138828286" t="2"\zwd*. 
\v 19 When \zwd Azubah|id="Q139582293" t="2"\zwd* died, \zwd Caleb|id="Q16938772" t="2"\zwd* married \zwd Ephrath|id="Q1296510" t="2"\zwd*,\f + \fr 2:19 \ft Ephrath is a variant of Ephrathah; see verse 50.\f* who bore to him \zwd Hur|id="Q492665" t="2"\zwd*. 
\v 20 \zwd Hur|id="Q492665" t="2"\zwd* was the father of \zwd Uri|id="Q66919839" t="2"\zwd*, and \zwd Uri|id="Q66919839" t="2"\zwd* was the father of \zwd Bezalel|id="Q853439" t="2"\zwd*. 
\b
\li1 
\v 21 Later, \zwd Hezron|id="Q4177234" t="2"\zwd* slept with \zwd the daughter of \zwd Machir the father of \zwd Gilead|id="Q85853273" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q85854026" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q85853398" t="2"\zwd*. He had married her when he was sixty years old, and she bore to him \zwd Segub|id="Q85854804" t="2"\zwd*. 
\v 22 \zwd Segub|id="Q85854804" t="2"\zwd* was the father of \zwd Jair|id="Q85853544" t="2"\zwd*, who had twenty-three cities in the land of Gilead. 
\v 23 But \zwd Geshur|\zwd* and \zwd Aram|\zwd* captured Havvoth-jair,\f + \fr 2:23 \ft Or the villages of Jair\f* along with Kenath and its sixty surrounding villages. All these were descendants of \zwd Machir the father of \zwd Gilead|id="Q85853273" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q85854026" t="2"\zwd*. 
\b
\li1 
\v 24 After \zwd Hezron|id="Q4177234" t="2"\zwd* died in Caleb-ephrathah, his wife \zwd Abijah|\zwd* bore \f + \fr 2:24 \ft Or After Hezron died, Caleb had relations with Ephrathah, the wife of Hezron his father, and she bore; see also LXX.\f* to him \zwd Ashhur the father \f + \fr 2:24 \ft Or the founder; also in verses 42, 45, 49, and possibly elsewhere\f* of \zwd Tekoa|id="Q115481221" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q115481149" t="2"\zwd*. 
