\c 3
\s1 The Descendants of David
\r (2 Samuel 3:1–5)
\m 
\v 1 These were the sons of \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* who were born to him in Hebron: 
\b
\li1 The firstborn was \zwd Amnon|id="Q361636" t="2"\zwd* by \zwd Ahinoam of Jezreel|id="Q400266" t="2"\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 the second was \zwd Daniel|\zwd* by \zwd Abigail of Carmel|id="Q4416778" t="2"\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 2 the third was \zwd Absalom the son of \zwd Maacah daughter of \zwd King Talmai of Geshur|\zwd*|id="Q11765188" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q205372" t="2"\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 the fourth was \zwd Adonijah the son of \zwd Haggith|id="Q5638717" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q360378" t="2"\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 
\v 3 the fifth was \zwd Shephatiah|id="Q9351247" t="2"\zwd* by \zwd Abital|id="Q33026741" t="2"\zwd*; 
\b
\li1 and the sixth was \zwd Ithream|id="Q11727237" t="2"\zwd* by \zwd his wife Eglah|id="Q12630462" t="2"\zwd*. 
\b
\li1 
\v 4 \zwd These six sons|\zwd* were born to \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* in Hebron, where he reigned seven years and six months. 
\b
\m And \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd* reigned in Jerusalem thirty-three years, 
\v 5 and these sons were born to him in Jerusalem: 
\b
\li1 \zwd Shimea|id="Q133263412" t="2"\zwd*,\f + \fr 3:5 \ft Shimea is a variant of Shammua; see 2 Samuel 5:14 and 1 Chronicles 14:4.\f* \zwd Shobab|id="Q9352021" t="2"\zwd*, \zwd Nathan|id="Q3437128" t="2"\zwd*, and \zwd Solomon|id="Q37085" t="2"\zwd*. These four were born to him by \zwd Bathsheba \f + \fr 3:5 \ft One Hebrew manuscript and Vulgate (see also LXX and 2 Samuel 11:3); most Hebrew manuscripts Bath-shua\f* daughter of \zwd Ammiel|id="Q13408496" t="2"\zwd*|id="Q272277" t="2"\zwd*.\f + \fr 3:5 \ft Ammiel is a variant of Eliam; see 2 Samuel 11:3.\f* 
\b
\li1 
\v 6 \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd*’s other sons were \zwd Ibhar|id="Q5984013" t="2"\zwd*,\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Hebrew does not include David’s other sons were.\f* \zwd Elishua|id="Q132170354" t="2"\zwd*,\f + \fr 3:6 \ft Two Hebrew manuscripts (see also 2 Samuel 5:15 and 1 Chronicles 14:5); most Hebrew manuscripts Elishama\f* \zwd Eliphelet|id="Q132170591" t="2"\zwd*, 
\v 7 \zwd Nogah|\zwd*, \zwd Nepheg|id="Q133258642" t="2"\zwd*, \zwd Japhia|id="Q128310030" t="2"\zwd*, 
\v 8 \zwd Elishama|\zwd*, \zwd Eliada|id="Q9252681" t="2"\zwd*, and \zwd Eliphelet|\zwd*—nine in all. 
\b
\li1 
\v 9 These were all the sons of \zwd David|id="Q41370" t="2"\zwd*, besides the sons by his concubines. And \zwd Tamar|id="Q2917173" t="2"\zwd* was their sister. 
\s1 The Descendants of Solomon
\b
\li1 
